//? Title: Iterative Deepening DFS: Shallowest Paths and Repeated Work
//? Subtitle: Actual depth-limited passes on finite directed graphs
//? Exports: both
//? Lang: en-GB

\abstract(
Find a path with the fewest edges in a directed unweighted graph without keeping
a breadth-first frontier. Iterative deepening repeats depth-first search with
limits zero, one and so on, stopping at the first goal. We preserve the original
two-vertex example, expose actual visits and cutoffs, derive the repeat-work
formula for complete trees and show why chain overhead is different. The kernel
now uses explicit heap frames and stops safely at the finite simple-path bound,
including when the requested depth is SIZE_MAX. Its stored graph and membership
array are accounted for separately from its active path.
)
\toc

> Start with the original edge

The original example has vertices zero and one, the directed edge zero to one,
source zero, goal one and maximum depth one. Its earlier program returned only
an exit status. The same call still succeeds; now we print the actual path and
counter. At limit zero the start is entered and cut off. At limit one the start
is entered again and the goal is entered. The historical `expanded` total is
therefore three, even though the graph has only two distinct vertices and only
one adjacency entry was examined. A goal is checked before the cutoff rule.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/iddfs_tiny.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/iterative_deepening_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const auto original =
        dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs(2, {{0, 1}}, 0, 1, 1);
    const auto h =
        dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_trace(2, {{0, 1}}, 0, 1, 1);
    std::print("Original path {}, found {}, cumulative entries {}.\n",
               original.path, original.found, original.expanded);
    std::print("| limit | actual entries | examined arcs | cutoffs | maximum stack | found |\n| ---: | ---: " "| ---: | ---: | ---: | --- |\n");
    for (const auto &p : h.run.passes)
        std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {} |\n", p.limit, p.entered,
                   p.edges_examined, p.cutoffs, p.maximum_stack, p.found);
    dm::algorithms::deepening_pass_diagram(h.run).save_svg(
        "build/iddfs_tiny.svg");
}
```
