> Derive repeat-work overhead and its assumptions

In a complete b-ary tree with a last-visited goal at depth d, the final pass
enters \(S_d=\sum_{k=0}^d b^k\) vertices. A level-k vertex is entered in passes
k through d, exactly d−k+1 times. Summing by level gives

$$
V_d=\sum_{k=0}^d(d-k+1)b^k.
$$
\alttext(Total iterative-deepening entries count each level-k vertex once for every pass from k through d.)

For b>1, exchanging the sums or differentiating the geometric series yields

$$
S_d=\frac{b^{d+1}-1}{b-1},\qquad
V_d=\frac{b^{d+2}-(d+2)b+(d+1)}{(b-1)^2},\qquad
\frac{V_d}{S_d}\longrightarrow\frac{b}{b-1}.
$$
\alttext(Complete branching trees have a finite asymptotic repeat-entry factor b divided by b minus one relative to one complete final pass.)

For b=1 the tree is a chain: \(S_d=d+1\), but \(V_d=(d+1)(d+2)/2\), so the ratio
is \((d+2)/2\) and grows without bound. These formulas count entered prefixes,
not CPU time, adjacency examinations or all possible graphs. In a graph, many
simple prefixes can end at the same vertex; in a multigraph, parallel arcs can
repeat even those prefixes. A constant overhead claim needs the exponential-tree
assumptions, not merely a finite stored graph.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/iddfs_overhead.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/iterative_deepening_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    std::vector<double> depths, chain, binary, ternary;
    std::print("| depth | branching | complete vertices | final-pass entries | total entries | entry ratio " "|\n| ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: | ---: |\n");
    for (std::size_t d = 1; d <= 8; ++d) {
        depths.push_back(d);
        for (std::size_t b : {1, 2, 3}) {
            const auto t = dm::algorithms::deepening_tree(b, d);
            const auto r =
                dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_run(t.n, t.edges, 0,
                                                            t.goal, t.depth);
            const double ratio =
                double(r.result.expanded) / r.passes.back().entered;
            std::print("| {} | {} | {} | {} | {} | {:.8g} |\n", d, b, t.n,
                       r.passes.back().entered, r.result.expanded, ratio);
            (b == 1 ? chain : b == 2 ? binary : ternary).push_back(ratio);
        }
    }
    auto p = dm::graphics::RPlot::create();
    p.line(depths, chain, "chain b=1", {220, 38, 38}, 2).line(depths, binary,
                                                              "binary b=2",
                                                              {37, 99, 235}, 2).line(depths, ternary, "ternary b=3", {22, 163, 74}, 2).title("Repeat-work ratio: chains differ from branching trees").x_label("goal depth").y_label("total entries / final-pass entries").y_limits(0, 6).save_svg("build/iddfs_overhead.svg");
}
```
