\caption(All ratios use actual producing counters; the chain grows while branching-tree ratios approach two and one-and-a-half.)
\alttext(Actual entry ratios for depths one through eight: the unary chain rises to five, binary approaches two and ternary approaches one-and-a-half.)

> Path-local cycle exclusion, budgets and real storage

The next graph has arcs 0→1→2→3 and 0→3→4→5, with goal five. In the limit-three
pass, vertex three is first reached at the cutoff through 0,1,2,3. It must then
be allowed again through the shorter prefix 0,3, continuing to 4,5. A single
pass-wide visited flag would incorrectly prune this valid depth-three solution.
The actual trace enters vertex three twice in that pass.

The explicit stack contains at most D+1 frames, each retaining a vertex, next
adjacency position and incoming original edge id. The implementation also stores
O(n+E) adjacency, an O(n) membership array, O(D+1) pass summaries and the owned
answer. The original unqualified O(d) space claim therefore describes only the
active path, not this stored-graph implementation's total memory. Optional trace
input copies/events add storage proportional to what is retained.

Complete terminal and original endpoint validation precedes caps/allocation,
including unreachable components and start-equals-goal calls. New run/trace
policies default to one million complete vertices, original edges and retained
scalar events each; zero disables the respective optional cap. Loops and
parallel arcs count toward the original edge cap. Event admission is checked
before each append; failure returns no partial trace. This cap excludes pass
summaries, input copies, adjacency, membership/frames, counters, scalar
metadata, capacity and byte/peak RAM. Untraced calls ignore the event cap; the
legacy entry point disables optional caps. All returned paths, arcs and events
own their values.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/iddfs_controls.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <datamunge/algorithms/iterative_deepening_analysis.hpp>
#include <filesystem>
#include <print>
#include <stdexcept>
int main() {
    std::filesystem::create_directories("build");

    const std::vector<std::pair<std::size_t, std::size_t>> edges{{0, 1}, {1, 2},
                                                                 {2, 3}, {0, 3},
                                                                 {3, 4}, {4, 5}};
    const auto h =
        dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_trace(6, edges, 0, 5, 3);
    std::size_t repeated = 0;
    for (const auto &e : h.events)
        if (e.kind == dm::algorithms::DeepeningEventKind::enter &&
            e.limit == 3 && e.vertex == 3)
            ++repeated;
    const auto bounded =
        dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_run(3, {{0, 1}, {1, 0}}, 0, 2,
                                                    std::numeric_limits<
                                                    std::size_t>::max());
    std::print("| control | observed |\n| --- | --- |\n| depth-three path | {} |\n| vertex-three entries at " "limit three | {} |\n| SIZE_MAX request effective depth | {} |\n| failed bounded passes | {} " "|\n| exact event admission | {} |\n",
               h.run.result.path, repeated, bounded.effective_max_depth,
               bounded.passes.size(), h.events.size());
    (void) dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_trace(6, edges, 0, 5, 3,
                                                         {6, 6, h.events.size()});
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs_trace(
            6, edges, 0, 5, 3, {6, 6, h.events.size() - 1});
        throw std::runtime_error("event cap accepted");
    } catch (const std::length_error &) {
        std::print("| one-short complete event cap | rejected |\n");
    }
    try {
        (void) dm::algorithms::iterative_deepening_dfs(3, {{2, 3}}, 0, 0, 0);
        throw std::runtime_error("unused invalid arc accepted");
    } catch (const std::invalid_argument &) {
        std::print("| invalid unused endpoint despite start=goal | rejected |\n");
    }
    dm::algorithms::deepening_pass_diagram(h.run).save_svg(
        "build/iddfs_controls.svg");
}
```
